      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment through **credential scoping**:\n\n1. **The key never enters the Hub\u0027s environment**: A local secrets loader reads the API key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup, but keeps it separate from the Hub\u0027s process environment.\n\n2. **Injection at spawn time**: The key is injected only into the environment of spawned child processes (the Ingest agent and Query agent) immediately before they start.\n\n3. **Hub\u0027s environment remains unmodified**: The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated, so a compromised or misbehaving Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its environment variables.\n\n4. **Short-lived child processes hold the credential**: The API key exists only in the short-lived child processes that actually call the Anthropic API, not in the Hub itself.\n\nThis design isolates the credential to the processes that actually need it, reducing the attack surface if the Hub process were to be compromised.",
